.TH http_request_new 3 "HTTP Library Functions" "QuickJS" "HTTP Library Functions"

.SH NAME
http_request_new \- Create a new HTTP request

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/http.h>
.B http_request* http_request_new(http* h);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The .B http_request_new function creates a new HTTP request.

The function takes one parameter:
.I h
The HTTP structure.

The function returns a pointer to the new HTTP request, or NULL on error.

.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the .B http_request_new function:

.I
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/http.h>

int main() {
  // Assume h is a valid HTTP structure
  http h;

  // Initialize h

  http_request* req = http_request_new(&h);

  if (!req) {
    perror("http_request_new");
    return 1;
  }

  // Use the new HTTP request

  return 0;
}
.!
